WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.800
Within loops, there may be a time in which&nbsp;
you need to have a condition for exiting a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.320
loop early. Using the previous code example&nbsp;
as a guide, I have added a platinum coin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:16.320
to a player's list of coins. Players collect&nbsp;
coins by answering questions correctly. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.080
are automatically moved to the next level if they&nbsp;
obtain a platinum coin. Thus, we want this code,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:29.680
the 223-break file, to stop and print a different&nbsp;
message if the player gets a platinum coin. I will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:40.040
add an if statement on line 4 to see if the&nbsp;
coin is Platinum. Remember that criteria are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:51.040
case-sensitive. I will then indent line 5 and add&nbsp;
a congratulatory print statement. The new keyword,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:57.320
break, I will add to line 6. Break exits&nbsp;
a loop. We are saying logically here that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:02.560
if a player obtains a platinum coin, no other&nbsp;
coins matter as the player automatically gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:08.000
moved to the next level. Here is a question:&nbsp;
how many statements do you think will print&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:18.080
when we run this code? Let’s find out. The&nbsp;
code prints four statements. The first three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.440
statements represent getting through the&nbsp;
first three coins in the coins tuple. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.280
being that the third coin is platinum, the&nbsp;
congratulatory statement prints, and then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:36.360
because of the break line, the loop ends before&nbsp;
it gets to the gold coin. The real-life gaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.840
application is that the gold coin is irrelevant&nbsp;
after the platinum coin and thus does not need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.720
to be displayed. Break statements break out of&nbsp;
loops when required and prevent one from adding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:53.640
multiple conditional statements to break out of a&nbsp;
loop, saving time and potential errors in logic.

